From 101ab74a8b7b53377c76af78896643ff29d16cda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:39:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] Today's physiotherapy: the protocol exercises and the
 pain

Patients followed by a physiotherapist get "Today's physiotherapy" on the
follow-up card. It shows the published protocols of the day from the
server's day view: each exercise with sets, repetitions, time, load, where
to do it, the instructions and the video link, and "Mark as done"
(an exercise record; "Done today" afterwards). Below, the pain on the
0 to 10 scale at one of the moments the physiotherapist asks for (or
another moment), with optional place and notes; it feeds the pain alerts
of the physiotherapist. Today's pain records are listed under the form.

The new feature is named physio, after the Django app.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VRSTuUkoebWWM2DLbPZAvR
